s  or insulating our homes so sam do you  welcome this private investment into  technological research i mean how much  of a role should private capital be  playing or really should it be the job  of governments to fund developments that  will benefit us all in the long run  i mean i think private capital uh has  has a huge role and we know that this  transition to net zero globally is going  to be very capital intensive it's going  to require lots of new infrastructure  lots of new um techniques and  forms of businesses which we know will  require investment and it's too much i  think for any government  to fund and to finance exclusively so  the private sector has got a really key  role and so i absolutely welcome welcome  this fund and i think you know you're  right to say that there are some easy  readily deployable uh solutions which  are available now things like wind solar  which have come down a lot in cost in  recent decades it's absolutely right  that we keep deploying those at scale  but we do also need new technologies and  cheaper technologies and some of the  hard to decarbonize sectors like  aviation like the negative emissions so  that's where i think the real value of  this fund will come from  and technology judy does have a big part  to play in tackling climate change  doesn't it potentially but do you think  the money is heading in the right  direction i mean talking about aviation  fuel for example do you think that's the  right area that we should be focusing on  at the moment  i really want the massive amounts of  money floating around going into things  that are really fundamental to the  center of people's lives you talk about  massive investment initiatives focusing  on lowering green premiums on aviation  does not appeal to me because it's not  sustainable to encourage more flying and  some time ago i heard that the jet  setting habits of bill gates and paris  hilton mean that they produce an  astonishing 10 000 times more carbon  emission